cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "pchic_gat: Contact Topology Alone — A Promoter-Centred Sequence-Structure Fusion Network for Multi-Task Prediction of Gene Regulatory State from Promoter Capture Hi-C Loop Calls"
authors:
  - family-names: Sengupta
    given-names: Kaustav
    email: rish.kaustav@gmail.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/Kaustav-93/pchic_gat"
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-08-26"
abstract: >
  Promoter-anchored PCHi-C / Hi-C subgraphs + promoter sequence + histone marks
  fused into two embedding spaces, evaluated across four supervised heads with
  5-fold gene-grouped cross-validation. Companion code for the paper "Contact
  Topology Alone: A Promoter-Centred Sequence-Structure Fusion Network for
  Multi-Task Prediction of Gene Regulatory State from Promoter Capture Hi-C
  Loop Calls".
keywords:
  - promoter capture Hi-C
  - graph attention network
  - gene regulation
  - Hi-C
  - genomics
  - HyenaDNA
